## Control {{controlId}}: Control and Monitor the Use of Mobile Code

**Implementation Status:** {{status}}

This organization controls and monitors mobile code execution within the {{tenantName}} M365 GCC High tenant through application protection policies, endpoint security configurations, and code execution restrictions managed by {{variables.systemAdministrator}}.

{{#if appProtectionsActive}}
**Application Protection Policies:**
{{appProtectionsCount}} application protection policies restrict mobile code execution on managed and unmanaged devices:
- Managed apps enforce data loss prevention controls preventing unauthorized code execution
- Cut/copy/paste restrictions between managed and unmanaged applications
- Jailbreak/root detection blocks access from compromised devices capable of executing unauthorized mobile code
{{else}}
Application protection policies have not been configured. Mobile code restrictions on managed applications are not enforced.
{{/if}}

**Endpoint Code Execution Controls:**
- PowerShell execution policies restrict script execution to signed scripts from trusted publishers
- Windows Defender Application Control (WDAC) policies enforce application allowlisting on managed endpoints
- Microsoft Defender for Endpoint monitors and blocks suspicious script execution (JavaScript, VBScript, macro-enabled documents)
- Browser security policies disable unauthorized ActiveX, Java applets, and browser extensions

{{#if securityAlertsActive}}
**Mobile Code Monitoring:**
{{securityAlertsCount}} security alert rules detect unauthorized mobile code activity, including malicious macro execution, unauthorized script invocation, and suspicious application behavior.
{{/if}}

**Responsible Party:** {{variables.systemAdministrator}}

**Verification Method:** Examine application protection policies, WDAC configurations, PowerShell execution policies, Defender alert rules for code execution, and endpoint security baselines.

